:{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111380","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111380","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111380.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111380.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Resolves https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13338\r\n\r\nAdded new `ClipChildrenMode` to editor. This change allows rendering any `CanvasItem` as a `CanvasGroup`. With this feature implemented, we get convenient `CanvasGroup` rendering not only for `Node2D` but for `Control` as well, without introducing any additional nodes. \r\n\r\nI am not sure about the name of the new `ClipChildrenMode` though. Is \"CanvasGroup\" okay? Other options I have in mind are \"transparent\" (similar to the respective [CanvasGroupMode](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_renderingserver.html#enum-renderingserver-canvasgroupmode)) and \"isolate\".","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111380/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":12,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111380/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}